{"causes": ["The devastating defeat of the Teutonic Knights at the Battle of Grunwald in 1410 profoundly weakened the Order's military and financial stability, creating a crisis for subsequent Grand Masters.", "The onerous war indemnities imposed by the First Peace of Thorn in 1411 placed immense financial pressure on the Teutonic Order, necessitating drastic measures by its leadership.", "The deposition of Grand Master Heinrich von Plauen in 1414 created a power vacuum and a mandate for a new leader to stabilize the Teutonic Order."], "effects": ["Michael Küchmeister's policies led to further financial distress and internal discontent within the Teutonic Order due to heavy taxation and asset sales.", "His leadership during the Gollub War resulted in the Treaty of Melno (1422), which permanently ceded Samogitia and other territories to Lithuania, marking a significant territorial loss for the Order.", "The continued military and diplomatic setbacks under Küchmeister contributed to the irreversible decline of the Teutonic Order's power and influence in Central Europe."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "teutonic-knights", "sourceName": "Teutonic Knights", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "michael-kchmeister-von-sternberg", "targetName": "Michael Küchmeister von Sternberg", "context": "Michael Küchmeister von Sternberg served as the 28th Grand Master of the Teutonic Knights from 1414 to 1422."}, {"sourceSlug": "battle-of-grunwald", "sourceName": "Battle of Grunwald", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "michael-kchmeister-von-sternberg", "targetName": "Michael Küchmeister von Sternberg", "context": "The devastating defeat of the Teutonic Knights at the Battle of Grunwald in 1410 profoundly influenced the challenging political and financial landscape Michael Küchmeister inherited as Grand Master."}, {"sourceSlug": "michael-kchmeister-von-sternberg", "sourceName": "Michael Küchmeister von Sternberg", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "gollub-war", "targetName":